(26345: (meta: (t: semantic) (n: 1) (term: string%20value) (def: Import%20named%20and%20referenced%20schema%20constraints%20and%20emit%20interoperable%20decoder%20grammars.%20Lower%20exclusive%20alternatives%20with%20disjoint%20instance%20types%20exactly%20and%20report%20unsupported%20constraints.%20Match%20supported%20string%20patterns%20against%20decoded%20Unicode%20scalars%20regardless%20of%20their%20JSON%20escape%20spelling.%20Validation%20preserves%20syntax%20links%2C%20UTF-8%20spans%20and%20pointers%20at%20schema%20violations%20and%20malformed%20JSON.%20Emit%20the%20original%20schema%20or%20infer%20a%20schema%20from%20bounded%20finite%20productions.%20Date%2C%20date-time%2C%20UUID%20and%20email%20decoder%20rules%20recognize%20their%20supported%20formats%20across%20direct%20and%20escaped%20JSON%20spellings.%20A%20pattern%20surrogate-pair%20escape%20matches%20one%20Unicode%20scalar%2C%20including%20in%20character%20ranges%20and%20repetitions.%20Object%20constants%20and%20enumerated%20objects%20within%20the%20decoder%20member%20limit%20accept%20permutations%20with%20the%20same%20keys%20and%20values%2C%20including%20nested%20objects.%20Overlapping%20integer%20alternatives%20admit%20integer%20spellings%20that%20match%20exactly%20one%20interval%20and%20report%20alternate%20decimal%20and%20exponent%20spellings.%20Object%20alternatives%20are%20exact%20when%20disjoint%20allowed%20strings%20for%20a%20shared%20required%20property%20distinguish%20each%20pair%2C%20and%20retain%20diagnostics%20when%20optional%20or%20overlapping%20tags%20cannot%20distinguish%20the%20branches.%20Recognized%20string%20formats%20combine%20with%20supported%20regular%20patterns%20over%20decoded%20strings%2C%20with%20an%20impossible%20conjunction%20producing%20no%20generatable%20grammar.%20Finite%20local%20references%20and%20nested%20alternatives%20enforce%20supported%20sibling%20assertions%20and%20exclusive%20branch%20counts.%20Validation%20uses%20the%20original%20JSON%20number%20spelling%20for%20integer%20types%2C%20four%20numeric%20bounds%2C%20and%20numbers%20in%20constants%20and%20enumerations%2C%20with%20precise%20UTF-8%20spans.%20Sibling%20type%20assertions%20restrict%20references%20and%20alternatives%2C%20including%20recursive%20references%20and%20the%20integer%20subset%20of%20numbers.%20Exclusive%20branch%20tests%20apply%20inside%20the%20restricted%20types.%20Supported%20overlapping%20string%20alternatives%20count%20exactly%20one%20match%20across%20patterns%2C%20formats%20and%20finite%20values%2C%20including%20sibling%20string%20constraints.%20String-only%20local%20references%20and%20inclusive%20alternatives%20intersect%20supported%20sibling%20patterns%20and%20formats%20with%20referenced%20and%20branch%20languages%2C%20with%20diagnosed%20fallback%20at%20the%20established%20work%20bound.%20Bounded%20local%20reference%20chains%20enforce%20regular%20string%20constraints%20and%20participate%20in%20exact%20alternatives%20distinguished%20by%20string%20languages%20or%20required%20object%20tags.%20Numeric%20decoder%20limits%20compose%20through%20local%20reference%20chains%20and%20constrain%20numeric%20inclusive%20alternatives%20and%20exclusive%20integer%20intervals.%20Object-only%20reference%20chains%20combine%20required%20names%20with%20a%20single%20property%20layout%2C%20including%20its%20additional-property%20policy.%20Array-only%20chains%20take%20the%20strongest%20length%20bounds%20around%20a%20single%20item%20layout.%20Impossible%20combinations%20have%20no%20generatable%20collection%20and%20unsupported%20layout%20intersections%20report%20a%20validation%20diagnostic.%20With%20a%20single%20property%20or%20item%20layout%20per%20branch%2C%20sibling%20length%20bounds%20and%20required%20names%20apply%20to%20every%20inclusive%20branch%20and%20to%20exclusive%20branches%20with%20disjoint%20instance%20types%20or%20required%20tags.%20A%20closed%20array%20tail%20bounds%20the%20decoder%20by%20the%20prefix%20length%20in%20the%20same%20schema%20object%2C%20including%20an%20empty%20prefix%20and%20impossible%20positive%20minima%20across%20references%20and%20alternatives.%20Object%2C%20array%2C%20string%20and%20numeric%20sibling%20assertions%20also%20apply%20within%20their%20instance%20types%20in%20mixed-type%20or%20untyped%20local%20references%20and%20inclusive%20alternatives%2C%20and%20in%20exclusive%20alternatives%20with%20disjoint%20referenced%20instance%20types.%20Compatible%20object%20layouts%20combine%20declared%20fields%20and%20apply%20each%20additional-property%20schema%20only%20to%20names%20outside%20its%20own%20declarations.%20Compatible%20array%20layouts%20compose%20position%20by%20position%2C%20using%20each%20layer%27s%20own%20prefix%20or%20tail%20schema.%20A%20forbidden%20item%20or%20disjoint%20declared%20types%20end%20the%20generatable%20prefix%20before%20the%20forbidden%20position.%20Additional-property%20defaults%20do%20not%20re-admit%20a%20declared%20property%20with%20disjoint%20types.%20Supported%20scalar%20assertions%20compose%20across%20property%20and%20item%20schemas%2C%20including%20local%20references%20to%20regular%20string%20constraints%20and%20inclusive%20numeric%20bounds.%20The%20same%20conjunction%20applies%20to%20additional%20property%20values%2C%20and%20type-scoped%20assertions%20permit%20unrelated%20instance%20types.%20When%20one%20property%20or%20item%20layer%20admits%20finitely%20many%20values%2C%20the%20decoder%20checks%20every%20candidate%20against%20all%20contributing%20schemas%2C%20including%20exclusive%20local%20alternatives%2C%20type-scoped%20numeric%20bounds%20and%20assertions%20on%20object%20members.%20An%20empty%20intersection%20forbids%20the%20property%20or%20item.%20Nested%20property%20and%20item%20collections%20combine%20compatible%20object%20and%20array%20layouts%20within%20a%20shared%20construction%20bound%2C%20with%20reported%20fallback%20on%20recursive%20intersections%20that%20reach%20the%20bound.%20Exclusive%20array%20alternatives%20with%20disjoint%20length%20intervals%20apply%20common%20sibling%20assertions%2C%20including%20intervals%20bounded%20by%20closed%20prefixes%20on%20local%20references.%20Overlapping%20length%20intervals%20with%20a%20shared%20item%20layout%20generate%20only%20lengths%20covered%20by%20exactly%20one%20branch.%20Unresolved%20intersections%20between%20different%20item%20layouts%20retain%20the%20exclusivity%20diagnostic.%20Exclusive%20array%20alternatives%20with%20overlapping%20lengths%20apply%20common%20sibling%20assertions%20when%20disjoint%20string%20sets%20distinguish%20a%20required%20position%20across%20local%20reference%20layers.%20An%20optional%20prefix%20cannot%20serve%20as%20that%20proof.%20Overlapping%20number-only%20alternatives%20apply%20joined%20limits%20and%20accept%20decimal%20spellings%20covered%20by%20exactly%20one%20branch%20across%20inclusive%20and%20open%20endpoints.%20When%20the%20exclusive%20intervals%20cover%20all%20numbers%2C%20exponent%20spellings%20remain%20generatable.%20Mixed%20integer%20and%20number%20alternatives%20count%20both%20kinds%20of%20branch%20for%20integral%20values%2C%20including%20zero-padded%20decimal%20spellings%2C%20and%20count%20only%20number%20branches%20for%20non-integral%20values.%20Supported%20string%20and%20numeric%20exclusivity%20applies%20independently%20within%20their%20instance%20types%20when%20other%20JSON%20instance%20types%20have%20separate%20alternatives.) (lang: meta-language%20structured%20data)))
